On Saturday morning, I go to the neighbourhood café.
I leave the dog, Moti, inside my home.
He must rest there.
I do my volunteer work at the café.
Then, I return home.
I stand in front of the door.
I slowly open the door.
Suddenly, Moti comes outside fast!
He quickly slips past me and runs into the hallway.
I place my bag on the floor.
"Moti, do not go there!" I say loudly.
"Come here quickly!"
He stops and looks at me.
"Sit right there!" I tell him.
I go near him and catch him.
"Moti, you must not do this," I say.
"You must not run in the hallway."
I take him back inside the home.
He is safe now, but my heart is beating fast.
